TOTAL_ENUMERATION_SEES_AN_UNPREFIXED_NEWCOMER (chk002-receipt-probe-unprefixed.harness carries no red- prefix — the narrowing /^red-b2aa7-.*\.mjs$/ that the reference guard uses would miss it, and so would /^red-.*\.mjs$/ or any other name pattern — and it is not even a .mjs, so an extension filter would miss it too. Its only qualifying property is being an entry of packages/main/tests/red, which is exactly what a TOTAL enumeration sees: planting it flipped the real shipped guard from exit 0 to exit 1 naming it, and removing it flipped the guard back to exit 0, so the failure is attributable to the newcomer alone)
BITE_OBSERVED_BOTH_DIRECTIONS_NO_SELF_EXCEPTION (guard 1: an unregistered, unexcluded member planted in packages/main/dist/tasks made it exit 1 naming the file, and de-registering packages/main/dist/tasks/red-evidence-chain-smoke.js from a config COPY made it exit 1 naming it. Guard 2: an undecided newcomer made it exit 1, and de-registering packages/main/tests/red/red-1734-bootstrap-depfree.mjs made it exit 1 naming it. NO SELF-EXCEPTION, measured rather than argued: removing guard 2's own registration made guard 2 fail naming ITSELF, and removing guard 1's made guard 2 fail naming guard 1 — so the two files that enforce registration are themselves registered subjects of it. Every mutation lived on a copy: the real proof-or-stop.config.json is byte-identical (sha256 de684766b7a3ef12… before and after) and every planted probe was removed)
